  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a persistent downward bias relative to true outcomes when recent history shows volatility and sentiment includes mixed signals (e.g., positive spikes followed by negative drops).",
    "When sentiment history contains a peak value of 1.00, the model significantly underestimates the subsequent price surge, failing to capture the full magnitude of the spike.",
    "The model displays excessive mean reversion bias; it predicts smoother, lower trajectories even when true outcomes show high-frequency oscillations around or above the forecasted path.",
    "In periods where sentiment shifts from positive (1.00) to negative (-1.00), the model fails to adjust its upward trajectory, resulting in a systematic under-forecast of volatility and peak levels.",
    "The 30-day horizon forecast consistently lags behind true outcomes by approximately 5-8 EUR during high-volatility regimes characterized by alternating sentiment extremes."
  ]
}
